#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:511
msgid "Checkout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:512
msgid "How the checkout delivery picker behaves. Reorder couriers by dragging their tabs above; prices show in the store currency."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:513
msgid "Default courier"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:514
msgid "Which courier is pre-selected at checkout (its first delivery option is the default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:516
msgid "Checkout dropdown results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:517
msgid "How many matches the city and street searches return. Office lists are never limited - the whole list for the chosen city is loaded. Raise it if customers report not finding their town; very high values make each keystroke slower on phones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:519
msgid "Preload city lists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:520
msgid "Embed each courier’s office/APS city list so those dropdowns open instantly. Address search stays live. Recommended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:521
msgid "Interactive map of all couriers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:522
msgid "Adds one map above the shipping methods showing every enabled courier’s offices and lockers for a city at once, with each courier’s price, so a customer can choose by where they will collect rather than by courier. Choosing a point fills in the courier, delivery type and office. Each courier keeps its own map button as well. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:524
msgid "“Nearest to you” on the map"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:525
msgid "On the interactive map, offer to find the customer’s location and then show how far each pickup point is, which one is closest, and what collecting there saves against delivery to the address. The distances are worked out in the customer’s own browser; their position is never stored on the site and is forgotten when they leave the page. The one time the coordinates leave the browser is when the customer presses “find me” before naming a town - those are then reverse-geocoded to fill the town in for them (see the External services notice). On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:527
msgid "Address map picker"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:528
msgid "Adds a “Choose on map” pin picker to address delivery that fills the address automatically. When a customer drops a pin, its coordinates are sent to OpenStreetMap Nominatim (or Google, if a key is set below) to look up the address. Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:529
msgid "Google Maps API key (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:530
msgid "Used for one thing only: turning a point picked on the map into an address. Leave it empty and OpenStreetMap Nominatim does that free of charge; the maps themselves are OpenStreetMap either way. The key needs Google’s “Geocoding API” and is only ever used from the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:532
msgid "Use the plugin’s own address fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:533
msgid "Remove WooCommerce’s Address / City / Region / Post code at checkout - the courier’s city, office or automat chosen here IS the delivery address, and asking twice lets the two disagree. Turn this off if your store also ships some other way and needs those fields. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:535
msgid "Hide the cart shipping calculator"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:536
msgid "Hide WooCommerce’s “Calculate shipping” box on the cart. It prices a delivery to a post code, while every price here is for the office, automat or address picked at checkout - so it would show a number the customer never pays. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:538
msgid "Require an e-mail address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:539
msgid "Insist on an e-mail address at checkout. The plugin makes the field optional by default - a courier waybill is built with the phone number, not with an e-mail - so turn this on if your shop needs the address for its own order e-mails or invoices. The phone number is always required. Do not also hide the e-mail field below: a required field nobody can see cannot be filled in, and the order cannot be placed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:541
msgid "Hide \"Country\" field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:542
msgid "Hidden checkout fields (CSS selectors)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:543
msgid "Comma-separated CSS selectors to hide on checkout (e.g. #billing_company_field, .cart-subtotal)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:548
msgid "Prices & display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:549
msgid "Shipping estimate on the cart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:550
msgid "On the cart page, show a rough cached shipping price per courier/option (the exact price is calculated at checkout). Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:551
msgid "Free shipping label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/class-bgcouriers-wc-settings.php:552
